Some parts of this project are taken from other projects with different
licences. Units of foreign source begin with a comment indicating their
source and the license that comes with it. Those licenses are distributed
with this project under the "licenses" directory.

Distributing this project as a whole need to satisfy all of those licenses'
requirements.

The text below is a commentary and has no legal value:

The intent behind choosing CC0 is to maximize flexibility. Regardless of the
license above, I wasn't going to sue you over this copyright, ever. So legally,
you were always in the clear. With CC0, it's even more explicit.

Regardless of the legal mumbo jumbo, this software has been created by humans as
a labor of love, so there's an emotional link to it. Omitting attribution has to
be done with what is commonly called "common sense".

There's a piece of code that you think is great and you want to use it elsewhere
without weighing your code with too much attribution mumbo jumbo? Sure, go
ahead. Nobody likes noise in the code, me first. A shoutout in the commit
comment would be great.

You want to strip the whole project of authorship marks and republish it as your
own? Sure, you're in the right. Nobody's going to sue you for it, nobody can sue
you for it. But know that this is generally seen as what is called a "dick move"
and makes you a special kind of person.

Therefore, this non-binding part of the license is a plea to humanity and common
sense.

